<section>
  <hgroup>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: January 4, 2026</p>
  </hgroup>

  <article>
    <h3>What We Collect</h3>
    <p><strong>Account Information:</strong> When you create an account, we collect your email address and password (securely hashed).</p>
    <p><strong>Photos:</strong> Photos you and your guests upload to galleries are stored on AWS S3 servers.</p>
    <p><strong>Usage Data:</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand how people use the site (page views, upload success, etc.).</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>How We Use Your Data</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide the photo sharing service</li>
      <li>To send you gallery links and important updates</li>
      <li>To improve the service based on usage patterns</li>
      <li>To prevent abuse and maintain security</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>We will never:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sell your data to third parties</li>
      <li>Use your photos for marketing or training AI models</li>
      <li>Share your email with advertisers</li>
      <li>Make your galleries public without your permission</li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>Data Storage & Security</h3>
    <p>Photos are stored on Amazon Web Services (AWS) S3 with AES-256 encryption at rest. Gallery links use unique identifiers that are not searchable or discoverable - only people with the link can access the gallery.</p>
    <p>Passwords are securely hashed using bcrypt before storage. Sessions are managed with encrypted cookies.</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>Your Rights</h3>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Delete any photo from your galleries</li>
      <li>Delete entire galleries and all associated photos</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your account and all data</li>
      <li>Export your data (contact us for assistance)</li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
    <p><strong>AWS S3:</strong> Photo storage (covered by AWS's privacy policy)</p>
    <p><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Anonymous usage tracking (you can opt-out with browser extensions)</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
    <p>We may update this policy as the service evolves. Significant changes will be communicated via email to registered users.</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h3>Contact</h3>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Email us at <a href="mailto:privacy@event-glimpse.com">privacy@event-glimpse.com</a></p>
  </article>

  <a href="/" role="button" class="outline">Back to Home</a>
</section>
